# The scenario responses are FIXTURES, not output.
#
# The repository root ignores `*.out` (line 142) because paid-session runners write .out files all over the
# tree. These six are recorded AWS responses that the replay reads, and without them three of its scenario
# directories do not exist at all -- so a fresh checkout loses 01, 02 and 06 and the harness reports "no
# scenario directory" for each.
#
# `git add` exited 0 while staging none of them. The miss was caught by reading the commit's own file list.
#
# The root .gitignore's own comment at line 131 records THIS EXACT ACCIDENT happening once before, to this
# same directory tree: "git add hack/test staged the driver and every golden file and silently left out the
# two files that make the harness a harness". The rule that was written down was not enough to stop it
# happening again, so the exemption lives here, beside the files it protects.
!*.out
!**/*.out
